    "result_text": "Done. The full build passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `membershipNumber` is a **derived** field \u2014 computed on every response from the owner's own `customerCode` and `registrationDate`, so no entity field, persistence, or pipeline step was needed.\n\nTwo small, cohesive changes:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` expression to the existing `toOwnerDto` method, matching the established pattern already used for the derived `displayName` and `initials`:\n   ```java\n   owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100)\n   ```\n   The `%02d` zero-pads the last two year digits (e.g. year 2026 \u2192 `26`, 2007 \u2192 `07`), producing `SMI-0007-M26`.\n\n**Structural impact kept low:** no method or class grew beyond a single added annotation line; the mapper interface method has CC 1 and its sibling methods carry little complexity. The computation reuses fields already set upstream (`AssignCustomerCode`, `BuildOwner`'s registration-date default), so it works identically on the create response and the `GET` re-fetch that the test exercises.",
